# Scoping Renovate to Specific Packages

This repo is a monorepo of multiple `apps/<app_type>/` applications (e.g.
`apps/python/`, `apps/java/`), each pinning dependencies against the private
Lightwell registry as their primary index/repository, which only hosts a
subset of packages per ecosystem (currently `PyYAML` and `Jinja2` for
Python). Renovate treats that primary registry as authoritative for every
package in the manifest, so any package Lightwell doesn't remediate (e.g.
`Flask`, `gunicorn`, `Pygments`) gets a 404 and fails lookup, even with a
fallback registry configured.

To keep Renovate scoped to only the packages Lightwell actually remediates,
disable each manager by default and re-enable it per-package, per-app-type
with `matchFileNames` + `matchPackageNames`. Renovate applies `packageRules`
in order and later matching rules override earlier ones, so list each
manager's disable rule before its enable rule:

```json
"packageRules": [
  {
    "matchManagers": ["pip_requirements"],
    "enabled": false
  },
  {
    "matchManagers": ["pip_requirements"],
    "matchFileNames": ["apps/python/**"],
    "matchDatasources": ["pypi"],
    "matchPackageNames": ["PyYAML", "Jinja2"],
    "enabled": true,
    "registryUrls": [
      "https://packages.redhat.com/lightwell/python/remediated/simple",
      "https://pypi.org/simple/"
    ]
  },
  {
    "matchManagers": ["maven"],
    "enabled": false
  }
]
```

Do not "fix" 404s by adding a catch-all `registryUrls` fallback to the
public registry for every package -- that reintroduces update PRs (e.g.
`pytest`, `Flask`) that are out of scope for the Lightwell remediation
workflow. When adding a new package to the Lightwell registry, add its name
to `matchPackageNames` in that app type's enable rule rather than relaxing
the default-disabled rule.

## Adding a new app type

1. Add the new manager to top-level `enabledManagers` (e.g. `"maven"`).
2. Add a `matchManagers: ["<manager>"], enabled: false` rule to disable it
   repo-wide by default (same pattern as `pip_requirements` above).
3. Add a scoped enable rule with `matchFileNames: ["apps/<type>/**"]` and
   `matchPackageNames` listing only the packages Lightwell remediates for
   that ecosystem.
4. `additionalBranchPrefix: "{{parentDir}}-"` (already set at the top level)
   splits Renovate PRs by the package file's parent directory, so each
   app type gets independent PRs/branches without extra per-type config.
